@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ito-il30-nouns`
IMPORT `ito-88-definitions`
IMPORT `ito-top-layer`
IMPORT `ito-91-capital-gains`

-- Tests for s 91 (the tax on a capital gain), paragraphs (a), (b), (b1), (b2), (c), (f), (g). Every expected value was worked by hand from the
-- section and from s 88's definitions (the arithmetic is beside each group) before it was run. A failing assertion is a finding.
-- All amounts are HYPOTHETICAL. The scales are fixtures: a FLAT scale (one band at 47%) makes the layering trivial where the test is about the
-- periods of (b1), and the scale of s 121(a)/(b)(1) is used where the test is about the layer.

§ `Tests of section 91`

§§ `Fixtures`

GIVEN u IS A NUMBER
      r IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A band of a marginal scale`
`a band ending at` u `at the rate` r MEANS
    `A band of a marginal scale` WITH
        `upper limit of the band` IS JUST u
        `rate of the band`        IS r

GIVEN r IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A band of a marginal scale`
`a last band at the rate` r MEANS
    `A band of a marginal scale` WITH
        `upper limit of the band` IS NOTHING
        `rate of the band`        IS r

`the scale of s 121(a)` MEANS
    LIST `a band ending at` 301_200 `at the rate` (31%),
         `a band ending at` 560_280 `at the rate` (35%),
         `a last band at the rate` (47%)

`the scale of s 121(b)(1)` MEANS
    LIST `a band ending at` 84_120 `at the rate` (10%),
         `a band ending at` 120_720 `at the rate` (14%),
         `a band ending at` 228_000 `at the rate` (20%),
         `a band ending at` 301_200 `at the rate` (31%),
         `a band ending at` 560_280 `at the rate` (35%),
         `a last band at the rate` (47%)

`a flat scale at 47%` MEANS LIST `a last band at the rate` (47%)

GIVEN f IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Holdings of means of control in one body of persons`
`a profits holding of` f MEANS
    `Holdings of means of control in one body of persons` WITH
        `fraction of the right to profits`                                              IS f
        `fraction of the right to appoint a director or general manager`                IS 0
        `fraction of the voting rights in the general meeting`                          IS 0
        `fraction of the right to a share of the surplus assets on winding up`          IS 0
        `fraction of the right to direct the holder of a right in (1) to (4) on how to use it` IS 0

GIVETH A LIST OF `A person who may hold together with the person`
`no others` MEANS EMPTY

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      f IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `The holdings of a person on one day`
`a profits record on` d `of` f MEANS
    `The holdings of a person on one day` WITH
        `the day` IS d
        `the person's own holdings that day` IS `a profits holding of` f
        `the others who may hold together with the person that day` IS `no others`

GIVETH A LIST OF `The holdings of a person on one day`
`no records` MEANS EMPTY

-- The readings: one builder, every fork named, and the default (everything declined).
GIVEN c  IS A `A reading of how the days of a period are counted`
      t  IS A `A reading of a cap on the rate where the gain stands in several bands`
      o  IS A `A reading of where each part of a gain stands in the top layer`
      v1 IS A `A reading of the years counted from 1949 in section 91(f)(1)`
      v2 IS A `A reading of the years counted from 2005 in section 91(f)(2)`
      v3 IS A `A reading of the real gain used for the middle part of a security bought before the fixed date`
      d2 IS A `A reading of the time at which section 91(b)(3) tests the shareholding`
      s4 IS A `A reading of the twelve months before a day`
GIVETH A `The readings of the forks in sections 88, 91, 125B and 125C`
`the readings: days` c `, cap` t `, places` o `, years from 1949` v1 `, years from 2005` v2 `, middle part` v3 `, (b)(3) time` d2 `, twelve months` s4 MEANS
    `The readings of the forks in sections 88, 91, 125B and 125C` WITH
        `together with another`                   IS `declined where the number of others changes the answer`
        `counting the days of a period`           IS c
        `half the holding expenses`               IS `declined where half the holding expenses changes the answer`
        `the twelve months before a day`          IS s4
        `the years from 1949 in section 91(f)(1)` IS v1
        `the years from 2005 in section 91(f)(2)` IS v2
        `a cap where the gain stands in several bands` IS t
        `where each part stands in the top layer` IS o
        `the time of the test in section 125B(3)` IS `declined where the time of the test changes the answer`
        `the time of the test in section 91(b)(3)` IS d2
        `the real gain for the middle part`       IS v3
        `the naming of a tax year of the Real Estate Taxation Law` IS `declined where the naming of the tax year changes the answer`

`the default readings` MEANS
    `the readings: days` `declined where the way of counting changes the answer` `, cap` `declined where the way of applying the cap changes the answer` `, places` `declined where the order of the parts changes the answer` `, years from 1949` `declined where the number of years changes the answer` `, years from 2005` `declined where the number of years changes the answer` `, middle part` `declined where the real gain used for the middle part changes the answer` `, (b)(3) time` `declined where the time of the sale test changes the answer` `, twelve months` `declined where the first day of the twelve months changes the answer`

-- The default except the days of a period, counted as named.
GIVEN c IS A `A reading of how the days of a period are counted`
GIVETH A `The readings of the forks in sections 88, 91, 125B and 125C`
`the default readings but the days counted as` c MEANS
    `the readings: days` c `, cap` `declined where the way of applying the cap changes the answer` `, places` `declined where the order of the parts changes the answer` `, years from 1949` `declined where the number of years changes the answer` `, years from 2005` `declined where the number of years changes the answer` `, middle part` `declined where the real gain used for the middle part changes the answer` `, (b)(3) time` `declined where the time of the sale test changes the answer` `, twelve months` `declined where the first day of the twelve months changes the answer`

-- The default except the years of (f), counted as named.
GIVEN v1 IS A `A reading of the years counted from 1949 in section 91(f)(1)`
      v2 IS A `A reading of the years counted from 2005 in section 91(f)(2)`
GIVETH A `The readings of the forks in sections 88, 91, 125B and 125C`
`the default readings but the years counted from 1949 as` v1 `and from 2005 as` v2 MEANS
    `the readings: days` `declined where the way of counting changes the answer` `, cap` `declined where the way of applying the cap changes the answer` `, places` `declined where the order of the parts changes the answer` `, years from 1949` v1 `, years from 2005` v2 `, middle part` `declined where the real gain used for the middle part changes the answer` `, (b)(3) time` `declined where the time of the sale test changes the answer` `, twelve months` `declined where the first day of the twelve months changes the answer`

-- The default except the middle part of a reduced security gain, read as named, with the days counted between.
GIVEN v3 IS A `A reading of the real gain used for the middle part of a security bought before the fixed date`
GIVETH A `The readings of the forks in sections 88, 91, 125B and 125C`
`the default readings with the days between and the middle part read as` v3 MEANS
    `the readings: days` `the days between the first day and the last day, the first not counted` `, cap` `declined where the way of applying the cap changes the answer` `, places` `declined where the order of the parts changes the answer` `, years from 1949` `declined where the number of years changes the answer` `, years from 2005` `declined where the number of years changes the answer` `, middle part` v3 `, (b)(3) time` `declined where the time of the sale test changes the answer` `, twelve months` `declined where the first day of the twelve months changes the answer`

-- The default except the time of the test in (b)(3), as named.
GIVEN d2 IS A `A reading of the time at which section 91(b)(3) tests the shareholding`
GIVETH A `The readings of the forks in sections 88, 91, 125B and 125C`
`the default readings but the (b)(3) time read as` d2 MEANS
    `the readings: days` `declined where the way of counting changes the answer` `, cap` `declined where the way of applying the cap changes the answer` `, places` `declined where the order of the parts changes the answer` `, years from 1949` `declined where the number of years changes the answer` `, years from 2005` `declined where the number of years changes the answer` `, middle part` `declined where the real gain used for the middle part changes the answer` `, (b)(3) time` d2 `, twelve months` `declined where the first day of the twelve months changes the answer`

-- A sale, with every field.
GIVEN seller IS A `The seller, for section 91`
      kind   IS A `The kind of asset sold, for section 91`
      lst    IS A BOOLEAN
      lstb   IS A BOOLEAN
      fund   IS A BOOLEAN
      rgain  IS A NUMBER
      cgain  IS A NUMBER
      cinfl  IS A NUMBER
      bought IS A DATE
      sold   IS A DATE
      isSec  IS A BOOLEAN
      prof   IS A NUMBER
      expro  IS A BOOLEAN
      yr     IS A NUMBER
      b2     IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A sale for section 91`
`the sale by` seller `of` kind `, listed` lst `, listed before the change date` lstb `, exempt fund unit` fund `, real gain` rgain `, capital gain` cgain `, chargeable inflationary` cinfl `, bought` bought `, sold` sold `, a security` isSec `, profits of 94B` prof `, expropriated` expro `, reached in` yr `, part of (b2)` b2 MEANS
    `A sale for section 91` WITH
        `the seller` IS seller
        `the kind of asset sold` IS kind
        `registered for trading on a stock exchange` IS lst
        `registered for trading on a stock exchange before the change date` IS lstb
        `a unit in an exempt mutual fund` IS fund
        `the real capital gain` IS rgain
        `the capital gain` IS cgain
        `the chargeable inflationary amount` IS cinfl
        `the purchase day` IS bought
        `the sale day` IS sold
        `the asset is a security` IS isSec
        `the distributable profits of section 94B deducted for a security bought before the fixed date` IS prof
        `the asset was expropriated` IS expro
        `the tax year in which the asset reached the seller` IS yr
        `the part of the real gain equal to depletion, exploration and development deductions or film production expenses on a unit in an oil or film partnership` IS b2

GIVEN recs IS A LIST OF `The holdings of a person on one day`
GIVETH A `The seller, for section 91`
`an individual with the records` recs MEANS `an individual` recs

GIVEN rate IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `The seller, for section 91`
`a body of persons taxed at` rate MEANS `a body of persons` rate

-- The ordinary individual's sale: no listing, no 94B, not expropriated, reached in the year of the purchase, nothing of (b2).
GIVEN seller IS A `The seller, for section 91`
      kind   IS A `The kind of asset sold, for section 91`
      rgain  IS A NUMBER
      cgain  IS A NUMBER
      cinfl  IS A NUMBER
      bought IS A DATE
      sold   IS A DATE
GIVETH A `A sale for section 91`
`an ordinary sale by` seller `of` kind `, real gain` rgain `, capital gain` cgain `, chargeable inflationary` cinfl `, bought` bought `, sold` sold MEANS
    `the sale by` seller `of` kind `, listed` FALSE `, listed before the change date` FALSE `, exempt fund unit` FALSE `, real gain` rgain `, capital gain` cgain `, chargeable inflationary` cinfl `, bought` bought `, sold` sold `, a security` FALSE `, profits of 94B` 0 `, expropriated` FALSE `, reached in` (DATE_YEAR bought) `, part of (b2)` 0

`the sale day of the tests` MEANS YMD 2026 6 30

§§ `Paragraph (b)(1): an individual`
-- Bought 1 May 2013 (after the change date): (b) alone. Other income 0, scale (a): the gain 200,000 lies in the 31% band, capped at 25%: 50,000.
--   With chargeable inflationary amount 20,000 (a hypothetical figure): + 10% = 2,000: 52,000.
#ASSERT `s 91 — the tax on` (`an ordinary sale by` (`an individual with the records` `no records`) `of` `any other asset` `, real gain` 200_000 `, capital gain` 300_000 `, chargeable inflationary` 0 `, bought` (YMD 2013 5 1) `, sold` `the sale day of the tests`) `, the seller's other taxable income being` 0 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` EQUALS 50_000
#ASSERT `s 91 — the tax on` (`an ordinary sale by` (`an individual with the records` `no records`) `of` `any other asset` `, real gain` 200_000 `, capital gain` 300_000 `, chargeable inflationary` 20_000 `, bought` (YMD 2013 5 1) `, sold` `the sale day of the tests`) `, the seller's other taxable income being` 0 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` EQUALS 52_000
-- Bought 1 January 2012, the change date itself: still (b) alone. Bought 31 December 2011: (b1). Same tax in (b) here: 50,000.
#ASSERT `s 91 — the tax on` (`an ordinary sale by` (`an individual with the records` `no records`) `of` `any other asset` `, real gain` 200_000 `, capital gain` 300_000 `, chargeable inflationary` 0 `, bought` (YMD 2012 1 1) `, sold` `the sale day of the tests`) `, the seller's other taxable income being` 0 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` EQUALS 50_000
-- A reduced-rate individual with the gain in the 10% band: 50,000 x 10% = 5,000.
#ASSERT `s 91 — the tax on` (`an ordinary sale by` (`an individual with the records` `no records`) `of` `any other asset` `, real gain` 50_000 `, capital gain` 80_000 `, chargeable inflationary` 0 `, bought` (YMD 2013 5 1) `, sold` `the sale day of the tests`) `, the seller's other taxable income being` 0 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(b)(1)` `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` EQUALS 5_000
-- Fork T1: other income 220,000, gain 100,000, scale (b)(1): 24,600 (each band capped) or 25,000 (average capped): refused by default.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 91 — the tax on` (`an ordinary sale by` (`an individual with the records` `no records`) `of` `any other asset` `, real gain` 100_000 `, capital gain` 150_000 `, chargeable inflationary` 0 `, bought` (YMD 2013 5 1) `, sold` `the sale day of the tests`) `, the seller's other taxable income being` 220_000 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(b)(1)` `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` BECAUSE "section 91 or section 88 leaves open a reading (the layer, the cap, the days of a period, who is a material shareholder, or the years of paragraph (f)), and here the tax turns on it"
#ASSERT `s 91 — the tax on` (`an ordinary sale by` (`an individual with the records` `no records`) `of` `any other asset` `, real gain` 100_000 `, capital gain` 150_000 `, chargeable inflationary` 0 `, bought` (YMD 2013 5 1) `, sold` `the sale day of the tests`) `, the seller's other taxable income being` 220_000 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(b)(1)` `, reading the forks as` (`the readings: days` `declined where the way of counting changes the answer` `, cap` `the rate of each band is capped` `, places` `declined where the order of the parts changes the answer` `, years from 1949` `declined where the number of years changes the answer` `, years from 2005` `declined where the number of years changes the answer` `, middle part` `declined where the real gain used for the middle part changes the answer` `, (b)(3) time` `declined where the time of the sale test changes the answer` `, twelve months` `declined where the first day of the twelve months changes the answer`) EQUALS 24_600

§§ `Paragraph (b)(2): a security in a body of persons sold by a material shareholder`
-- Other income 0, scale (a), gain 200,000 in the 31% band. A material shareholder (10% on the sale day): capped at 30%: 60,000.
-- Not a material shareholder (no records): capped at 25%: 50,000.
#ASSERT `s 91 — the tax on` (`an ordinary sale by` (`an individual with the records` (LIST `a profits record on` `the sale day of the tests` `of` (10%))) `of` `a security in a body of persons` `, real gain` 200_000 `, capital gain` 300_000 `, chargeable inflationary` 0 `, bought` (YMD 2013 5 1) `, sold` `the sale day of the tests`) `, the seller's other taxable income being` 0 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` EQUALS 60_000
#ASSERT `s 91 — the tax on` (`an ordinary sale by` (`an individual with the records` `no records`) `of` `a security in a body of persons` `, real gain` 200_000 `, capital gain` 300_000 `, chargeable inflationary` 0 `, bought` (YMD 2013 5 1) `, sold` `the sale day of the tests`) `, the seller's other taxable income being` 0 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` EQUALS 50_000
-- A record on 30 June 2025, exactly twelve months before the sale: inside one reading of the twelve months only. The tax is 60,000 or 50,000: refused.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 91 — the tax on` (`an ordinary sale by` (`an individual with the records` (LIST `a profits record on` (YMD 2025 6 30) `of` (10%))) `of` `a security in a body of persons` `, real gain` 200_000 `, capital gain` 300_000 `, chargeable inflationary` 0 `, bought` (YMD 2013 5 1) `, sold` `the sale day of the tests`) `, the seller's other taxable income being` 0 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` BECAUSE "section 91 or section 88 leaves open a reading (the layer, the cap, the days of a period, who is a material shareholder, or the years of paragraph (f)), and here the tax turns on it"
-- The same record, but the gain lies wholly in the 10% band (scale (b)(1)): 50,000 x 10% = 5,000 either way, so the unsettled status does not matter and the answer is given.
#ASSERT `s 91 — the tax on` (`an ordinary sale by` (`an individual with the records` (LIST `a profits record on` (YMD 2025 6 30) `of` (10%))) `of` `a security in a body of persons` `, real gain` 50_000 `, capital gain` 80_000 `, chargeable inflationary` 0 `, bought` (YMD 2013 5 1) `, sold` `the sale day of the tests`) `, the seller's other taxable income being` 0 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(b)(1)` `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` EQUALS 5_000

§§ `Paragraph (b)(3): a bond and the like not linked to the index`
-- The whole capital gain is regarded as real: CG 100,000 (the real gain figure 60,000 is not used); the chargeable inflationary amount 10,000 is not charged.
--   Not a material shareholder: 15% x 100,000 = 15,000. A material shareholder on the sale day: 20% x 100,000 = 20,000.
#ASSERT `s 91 — the tax on` (`an ordinary sale by` (`an individual with the records` `no records`) `of` `a bond, commercial security, loan note or loan that is not linked to the index` `, real gain` 60_000 `, capital gain` 100_000 `, chargeable inflationary` 10_000 `, bought` (YMD 2013 5 1) `, sold` `the sale day of the tests`) `, the seller's other taxable income being` 0 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` EQUALS 15_000
#ASSERT `s 91 — the tax on` (`an ordinary sale by` (`an individual with the records` (LIST `a profits record on` `the sale day of the tests` `of` (10%))) `of` `a bond, commercial security, loan note or loan that is not linked to the index` `, real gain` 60_000 `, capital gain` 100_000 `, chargeable inflationary` 10_000 `, bought` (YMD 2013 5 1) `, sold` `the sale day of the tests`) `, the seller's other taxable income being` 0 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` EQUALS 20_000
-- Fork D2: a record of 10% on 1 January 2026 only, six months before the sale. At the sale only: 15%. In the twelve months: 20%. Refused by default.
#ASSERT `s 91 — the tax on` (`an ordinary sale by` (`an individual with the records` (LIST `a profits record on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `of` (10%))) `of` `a bond, commercial security, loan note or loan that is not linked to the index` `, real gain` 60_000 `, capital gain` 100_000 `, chargeable inflationary` 0 `, bought` (YMD 2013 5 1) `, sold` `the sale day of the tests`) `, the seller's other taxable income being` 0 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, reading the forks as` (`the default readings but the (b)(3) time read as` `at the time of the sale only`) EQUALS 15_000
#ASSERT `s 91 — the tax on` (`an ordinary sale by` (`an individual with the records` (LIST `a profits record on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `of` (10%))) `of` `a bond, commercial security, loan note or loan that is not linked to the index` `, real gain` 60_000 `, capital gain` 100_000 `, chargeable inflationary` 0 `, bought` (YMD 2013 5 1) `, sold` `the sale day of the tests`) `, the seller's other taxable income being` 0 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, reading the forks as` (`the default readings but the (b)(3) time read as` `at the time of the sale or at some time in the twelve months before it`) EQUALS 20_000
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 91 — the tax on` (`an ordinary sale by` (`an individual with the records` (LIST `a profits record on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `of` (10%))) `of` `a bond, commercial security, loan note or loan that is not linked to the index` `, real gain` 60_000 `, capital gain` 100_000 `, chargeable inflationary` 0 `, bought` (YMD 2013 5 1) `, sold` `the sale day of the tests`) `, the seller's other taxable income being` 0 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` BECAUSE "section 91 or section 88 leaves open a reading (the layer, the cap, the days of a period, who is a material shareholder, or the years of paragraph (f)), and here the tax turns on it"

§§ `Paragraph (a): a body of persons, and paragraphs (c), (g) and (b2)`
-- A body of persons at a rate of 23% (an input; s 126 is not encoded): 200,000 x 23% = 46,000; with a chargeable inflationary amount of 20,000: + 2,000 = 48,000.
#ASSERT `s 91 — the tax on` (`an ordinary sale by` (`a body of persons taxed at` (23%)) `of` `any other asset` `, real gain` 200_000 `, capital gain` 300_000 `, chargeable inflationary` 0 `, bought` (YMD 2013 5 1) `, sold` `the sale day of the tests`) `, the seller's other taxable income being` 0 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` EQUALS 46_000
#ASSERT `s 91 — the tax on` (`an ordinary sale by` (`a body of persons taxed at` (23%)) `of` `any other asset` `, real gain` 200_000 `, capital gain` 300_000 `, chargeable inflationary` 20_000 `, bought` (YMD 2013 5 1) `, sold` `the sale day of the tests`) `, the seller's other taxable income being` 0 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` EQUALS 48_000
-- (g) expropriation: half the tax: 24,000.
#ASSERT `s 91 — the tax on` (`the sale by` (`a body of persons taxed at` (23%)) `of` `any other asset` `, listed` FALSE `, listed before the change date` FALSE `, exempt fund unit` FALSE `, real gain` 200_000 `, capital gain` 300_000 `, chargeable inflationary` 20_000 `, bought` (YMD 2013 5 1) `, sold` `the sale day of the tests` `, a security` FALSE `, profits of 94B` 0 `, expropriated` TRUE `, reached in` 2013 `, part of (b2)` 0) `, the seller's other taxable income being` 0 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` EQUALS 24_000
-- (g) for an individual: half of 50,000 = 25,000.
#ASSERT `s 91 — the tax on` (`the sale by` (`an individual with the records` `no records`) `of` `any other asset` `, listed` FALSE `, listed before the change date` FALSE `, exempt fund unit` FALSE `, real gain` 200_000 `, capital gain` 300_000 `, chargeable inflationary` 0 `, bought` (YMD 2013 5 1) `, sold` `the sale day of the tests` `, a security` FALSE `, profits of 94B` 0 `, expropriated` TRUE `, reached in` 2013 `, part of (b2)` 0) `, the seller's other taxable income being` 0 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` EQUALS 25_000
-- (b2): a part of the real gain equal to depletion deductions on a unit in an oil partnership. For a body of persons it changes nothing (s 126(a) either way): 46,000.
#ASSERT `s 91 — the tax on` (`the sale by` (`a body of persons taxed at` (23%)) `of` `any other asset` `, listed` FALSE `, listed before the change date` FALSE `, exempt fund unit` FALSE `, real gain` 200_000 `, capital gain` 300_000 `, chargeable inflationary` 0 `, bought` (YMD 2013 5 1) `, sold` `the sale day of the tests` `, a security` FALSE `, profits of 94B` 0 `, expropriated` FALSE `, reached in` 2013 `, part of (b2)` 80_000) `, the seller's other taxable income being` 0 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` EQUALS 46_000
-- For an individual the part's place in the scale is not said: declined.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 91 — the tax on` (`the sale by` (`an individual with the records` `no records`) `of` `any other asset` `, listed` FALSE `, listed before the change date` FALSE `, exempt fund unit` FALSE `, real gain` 200_000 `, capital gain` 300_000 `, chargeable inflationary` 0 `, bought` (YMD 2013 5 1) `, sold` `the sale day of the tests` `, a security` FALSE `, profits of 94B` 0 `, expropriated` FALSE `, reached in` 2013 `, part of (b2)` 80_000) `, the seller's other taxable income being` 0 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` BECAUSE "section 91(b2) taxes the part of an individual's gain equal to depletion deductions as in section 121, and does not say where that part stands in the scale"

§§ `The date`
-- A sale on 31 December 2011 is before the change date: declined. On 1 January 2012 (bought 1 May 2011 so that (b1) applies, flat scale) the answer needs (b1); see below.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 91 — the tax on` (`an ordinary sale by` (`an individual with the records` `no records`) `of` `any other asset` `, real gain` 200_000 `, capital gain` 300_000 `, chargeable inflationary` 0 `, bought` (YMD 2001 5 1) `, sold` (YMD 2011 12 31)) `, the seller's other taxable income being` 0 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` BECAUSE "the deposited text of section 91 is the text as amended to 2017, and the text for a sale before the change date, 1 January 2012, is not deposited"

§§ `Where the layered rates of (b1) apply`
GIVEN seller IS A `The seller, for section 91`
      kind   IS A `The kind of asset sold, for section 91`
      lst    IS A BOOLEAN
      lstb   IS A BOOLEAN
      fund   IS A BOOLEAN
      bought IS A DATE
