§§ `Paragraph (e): spreading (fixtures)`

GIVEN other  IS A NUMBER
      bands  IS A LIST OF `A band of a marginal scale`
      unused IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A tax year in the period of spreading`
`a year with other income` other `, scale` bands `, credit points left unused worth` unused MEANS
    `A tax year in the period of spreading` WITH
        `the other taxable income that year` IS other
        `the scale of section 121 for that year` IS bands
        `the value of the credit points left unused that year` IS unused

-- A sale of any other asset by an individual with no records, sold 30 June 2026, reaching the seller in the given tax year.
GIVEN yr IS A NUMBER
      rgain IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A sale for section 91`
`a spreading sale reached in` yr `with real gain` rgain MEANS
    `the sale by` (`an individual with the records` `no records`) `of` `any other asset` `, listed` FALSE `, listed before the change date` FALSE `, exempt fund unit` FALSE `, real gain` rgain `, capital gain` (rgain TIMES 2) `, chargeable inflationary` 0 `, bought` (YMD yr 5 1) `, sold` (YMD 2026 6 30) `, a security` FALSE `, profits of 94B` 0 `, expropriated` FALSE `, reached in` yr `, part of (b2)` 0

§§ `Paragraph (e)(1): four tax years`
-- Reached in 2013, sold in 2026: the period of ownership is 2014 to 2026, 13 years; the shorter of four and 13 is 4.
#ASSERT `s 91(e)(1) — the number of tax years for` (`a spreading sale reached in` 2013 `with real gain` 400_000) EQUALS 4
-- Reached in 2024, sold in 2026: the period is 2025 and 2026: 2 years.
#ASSERT `s 91(e)(1) — the number of tax years for` (`a spreading sale reached in` 2024 `with real gain` 200_000) EQUALS 2
-- Reached in 2023: 3 years. Reached in 2022: 4 years. Reached in 2021: 5 years, but four is the shorter.
#ASSERT `s 91(e)(1) — the number of tax years for` (`a spreading sale reached in` 2023 `with real gain` 1) EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `s 91(e)(1) — the number of tax years for` (`a spreading sale reached in` 2022 `with real gain` 1) EQUALS 4
#ASSERT `s 91(e)(1) — the number of tax years for` (`a spreading sale reached in` 2021 `with real gain` 1) EQUALS 4
-- Reached in the year of the sale: no year at all.
#ASSERT `s 91(e)(1) — the number of tax years for` (`a spreading sale reached in` 2026 `with real gain` 1) EQUALS 0
-- Real gain 400,000 over 4 years: 100,000 a year, above other income 0 under scale (a): 31% band, capped at 25%: 25,000 a year.
--   2023: 5,000 of credit points unused: 20,000. 2024: 30,000 unused: nothing (the tax cannot go below nought). 2025, 2026: 25,000 each. Total 70,000.
#ASSERT `s 91(e) — the tax on` (`a spreading sale reached in` 2013 `with real gain` 400_000) `spread over the years` (LIST `a year with other income` 0 `, scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, credit points left unused worth` 5_000, `a year with other income` 0 `, scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, credit points left unused worth` 30_000, `a year with other income` 0 `, scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, credit points left unused worth` 0, `a year with other income` 0 `, scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, credit points left unused worth` 0) `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` EQUALS 70_000
-- Two years: 200,000 over 2 = 100,000 each: 25,000 + 25,000 = 50,000. Three years given for two: declined.
#ASSERT `s 91(e) — the tax on` (`a spreading sale reached in` 2024 `with real gain` 200_000) `spread over the years` (LIST `a year with other income` 0 `, scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, credit points left unused worth` 0, `a year with other income` 0 `, scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, credit points left unused worth` 0) `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` EQUALS 50_000
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 91(e) — the tax on` (`a spreading sale reached in` 2024 `with real gain` 200_000) `spread over the years` (LIST `a year with other income` 0 `, scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, credit points left unused worth` 0, `a year with other income` 0 `, scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, credit points left unused worth` 0, `a year with other income` 0 `, scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, credit points left unused worth` 0) `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` BECAUSE "the number of tax years given is not the number of years over which section 91(e)(1) spreads the gain"
-- The year of the sale is the year it reached the seller: no period.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 91(e) — the tax on` (`a spreading sale reached in` 2026 `with real gain` 200_000) `spread over the years` (EMPTY) `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` BECAUSE "the period of ownership of section 91(e)(1) begins with the tax year after the year the asset reached the taxpayer, and here it gives no tax year"
-- (e)(3): a security registered for trading on a stock exchange is not spread.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 91(e) — the tax on` (`the sale by` (`an individual with the records` `no records`) `of` `a security in a body of persons` `, listed` TRUE `, listed before the change date` FALSE `, exempt fund unit` FALSE `, real gain` 200_000 `, capital gain` 300_000 `, chargeable inflationary` 0 `, bought` (YMD 2024 5 1) `, sold` (YMD 2026 6 30) `, a security` TRUE `, profits of 94B` 0 `, expropriated` FALSE `, reached in` 2024 `, part of (b2)` 0) `spread over the years` (LIST `a year with other income` 0 `, scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, credit points left unused worth` 0, `a year with other income` 0 `, scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, credit points left unused worth` 0) `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` BECAUSE "section 91(e)(3) does not apply paragraph (1), spreading, to a gain on a security registered for trading on a stock exchange"
-- A body of persons: not open.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 91(e) — the tax on` (`the sale by` (`a body of persons taxed at` (23%)) `of` `any other asset` `, listed` FALSE `, listed before the change date` FALSE `, exempt fund unit` FALSE `, real gain` 200_000 `, capital gain` 300_000 `, chargeable inflationary` 0 `, bought` (YMD 2024 5 1) `, sold` (YMD 2026 6 30) `, a security` FALSE `, profits of 94B` 0 `, expropriated` FALSE `, reached in` 2024 `, part of (b2)` 0) `spread over the years` (LIST `a year with other income` 0 `, scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, credit points left unused worth` 0, `a year with other income` 0 `, scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, credit points left unused worth` 0) `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` BECAUSE "section 91(e) spreads the tax computed at the rates of paragraph (b), which is an individual's, so it is not open to a body of persons"
-- An old asset, or one expropriated: not combined with (f) or (g) here.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 91(e) — the tax on` (`the sale by` (`an individual with the records` `no records`) `of` `any other asset` `, listed` FALSE `, listed before the change date` FALSE `, exempt fund unit` FALSE `, real gain` 200_000 `, capital gain` 300_000 `, chargeable inflationary` 0 `, bought` (YMD 1955 5 1) `, sold` (YMD 2026 6 30) `, a security` FALSE `, profits of 94B` 0 `, expropriated` FALSE `, reached in` 1955 `, part of (b2)` 0) `spread over the years` (EMPTY) `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` BECAUSE "this model does not combine the spreading of section 91(e) with paragraph (f), (g) or (b2): the text does not say how the caps and the halving fall on the years"
-- Fork T1 in a year: other income 220,000, share 100,000, scale (b)(1): 24,600 (each band capped) or 25,000 (the average capped): declined by default. Four such years with the cap read as each band: 4 x 24,600 = 98,400.
#ASSERT `s 91(e) — the tax on` (`a spreading sale reached in` 2013 `with real gain` 400_000) `spread over the years` (LIST `a year with other income` 220_000 `, scale` `the scale of s 121(b)(1)` `, credit points left unused worth` 0, `a year with other income` 220_000 `, scale` `the scale of s 121(b)(1)` `, credit points left unused worth` 0, `a year with other income` 220_000 `, scale` `the scale of s 121(b)(1)` `, credit points left unused worth` 0, `a year with other income` 220_000 `, scale` `the scale of s 121(b)(1)` `, credit points left unused worth` 0) `, reading the forks as` (`the readings: days` `declined where the way of counting changes the answer` `, cap` `the rate of each band is capped` `, places` `declined where the order of the parts changes the answer` `, years from 1949` `declined where the number of years changes the answer` `, years from 2005` `declined where the number of years changes the answer` `, middle part` `declined where the real gain used for the middle part changes the answer` `, (b)(3) time` `declined where the time of the sale test changes the answer` `, twelve months` `declined where the first day of the twelve months changes the answer`) EQUALS 98_400
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 91(e) — the tax on` (`a spreading sale reached in` 2013 `with real gain` 400_000) `spread over the years` (LIST `a year with other income` 220_000 `, scale` `the scale of s 121(b)(1)` `, credit points left unused worth` 0, `a year with other income` 220_000 `, scale` `the scale of s 121(b)(1)` `, credit points left unused worth` 0, `a year with other income` 220_000 `, scale` `the scale of s 121(b)(1)` `, credit points left unused worth` 0, `a year with other income` 220_000 `, scale` `the scale of s 121(b)(1)` `, credit points left unused worth` 0) `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` BECAUSE "section 91 or section 88 leaves open a reading (the layer, the cap, the days of a period, who is a material shareholder, or the years of paragraph (f)), and here the tax turns on it"

§§ `Paragraph (e)(2): spreading the three parts of (b1)`
-- Bought 2000, sold 2020 (so the sale day here is 1 January 2020 and the years are the four years 2017 to 2020): flat scale at 47%, every
-- part is linear in the layer, so the four years together tax the three parts exactly as the unspread tax does: 13,902,222.1 (days between).
--   one year with 1,000,000 of credit points unused: (13,902,222.1 / 4 = 3,475,555.525) - 1,000,000 = 2,475,555.525 ; one with 10,000,000: nothing ;
--   two with none: 3,475,555.525 each. Total 2,475,555.525 + 0 + 6,951,111.05 = 9,426,666.575.
GIVEN unusedlist IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF `A tax year in the period of spreading`
`four flat years with credit points left unused worth` unusedlist MEANS
    map (GIVEN u YIELD `a year with other income` 0 `, scale` `a flat scale at 47%` `, credit points left unused worth` u) unusedlist

`the old sale to spread` MEANS
    `an ordinary sale by` (`an individual with the records` `no records`) `of` `any other asset` `, real gain` 53_370_330 `, capital gain` 60_000_000 `, chargeable inflationary` 0 `, bought` (YMD 2000 1 1) `, sold` (YMD 2020 1 1)

#ASSERT `s 91(e)(1) — the number of tax years for` `the old sale to spread` EQUALS 4
#ASSERT `s 91(e) — the tax on` `the old sale to spread` `spread over the years` (`four flat years with credit points left unused worth` (LIST 0, 0, 0, 0)) `, reading the forks as` (`the default readings but the days counted as` `the days between the first day and the last day, the first not counted`) EQUALS 13_902_222.1
#ASSERT `s 91(e) — the tax on` `the old sale to spread` `spread over the years` (`four flat years with credit points left unused worth` (LIST 1_000_000, 10_000_000, 0, 0)) `, reading the forks as` (`the default readings but the days counted as` `the days between the first day and the last day, the first not counted`) EQUALS 9_426_666.575
-- Counting both ends: 13,903,387.35 over the four years.
#ASSERT `s 91(e) — the tax on` `the old sale to spread` `spread over the years` (`four flat years with credit points left unused worth` (LIST 0, 0, 0, 0)) `, reading the forks as` (`the default readings but the days counted as` `both the first and the last day are counted`) EQUALS 13_903_387.35
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 91(e) — the tax on` `the old sale to spread` `spread over the years` (`four flat years with credit points left unused worth` (LIST 0, 0, 0, 0)) `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` BECAUSE "section 91 or section 88 leaves open a reading (the layer, the cap, the days of a period, who is a material shareholder, or the years of paragraph (f)), and here the tax turns on it"
